      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's complex, but if you look at how they're used in practice, it feels like the \"democracy\" part is just a convenient excuse. like, if a country is actually behaving badly, why shouldn't we just call the sanctions what they are—a tool for major powers to maintain their dominance? if we're being honest, isn't it more accurate to say they're more about power than actual human rights?",
