      "role": "user",
      "content": "but isn't it kind of hypocritical then? like, we hear all this talk about \"defending democracy,\" but then we see sanctions being used against certain countries while others do way worse things but get a pass because they're allies. doesn't that mean the whole \"promoting democracy\" argument is just a facade for keeping the current global power structure in place? it feels like the \"pro-sanctions\" side is just ignoring the reality of how they're actually used.",
